OL,3,GNEWSABelfast Telegraph bomb victim
OL,4,Aremembered on 50th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe granddaughter of a Belfast
OL,7,FTelegraph worker killed 50 years ago in
OL,8,FNorthern Ireland says it is important
OL,9,Fto remember "forgotten" victims of
OL,10,Fviolence.
OL,12,FWhen the offices of the newspaper were
OL,13,Fbombed on 15 September 1976, it was the
OL,14,Fattack on the media that grabbed the
OL,15,Fheadlines.
OL,17,FFour days later, one of those injured
OL,18,Fin the blast, 63-year-old printer
OL,19,FJoseph Paton from Lisburn, died in
OL,20,Fhospital.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,414,410,260,120,0,100
